{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CfZpkR8FFzemRkHxHTEvn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on my analysis, I have a clear picture of what needs to be implemented.\n\n## Summary of findings:\n\n**Requirement**: Add a `POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm` endpoint that moves shipments from CREATED to CONFIRMED status, handles idempotency, and rejects cancelled/non-existent shipments with proper HTTP status codes.\n\n**Repository findings**:\n- Shipment entity (Shipment.kt:9-14) with ShipmentStatus enum (CREATED, CONFIRMED, CANCELLED)\n- ShipmentController (ShipmentController.kt:20) with create, getById, list endpoints\n- InMemoryShipmentRepository (ShipmentRepository.kt:10) with save, findById, existsById, findAll\n- Exception pattern: ResourceNotFoundException (404), ConflictException (409) thrown directly and handled by GlobalExceptionHandler (GlobalExceptionHandler.kt)\n- ErrorCode enum (ApiError.kt:31) with codes like SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND, SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS\n\n**Conventions**:\n- Spring MVC annotations for endpoints (@PostMapping, @PathVariable, @RequestBody)\n- Exceptions are thrown; GlobalExceptionHandler centrally converts to ApiError envelope\n- Repository methods are used to persist state\n- Tests use MockMvc with status().isOk/isConflict/isNotFound and jsonPath assertions\n\n**Affected files**:\n1. ShipmentController.kt - must add the confirm endpoint\n2. ApiError.kt - must add new ErrorCode for \"cancelled shipment cannot be confirmed\" error\n3. ShipmentControllerTest.kt - must add tests for the confirm functionality\n\n**Risks**:\n- Idempotency requirement: confirming already-confirmed must succeed without changes\n- Terminal state: cancelled shipment must reject with 409\n- Lost data: ensuring state persistence in repository\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n```\n\n**Proposed changes**:\n\n1. **ApiError.kt**: Add `SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS` to the ErrorCode enum to describe when a shipment is in an invalid state for the requested operation (specifically, when trying to confirm a cancelled shipment).\n\n2. **ShipmentController.kt**: Add a new POST endpoint method `confirm(@PathVariable shipmentId: String)` that:\n   - Finds the shipment; if not found, throws ResourceNotFoundException with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND (404)\n   - If status is CANCELLED, throws ConflictException with SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS (409)\n   - If status is already CONFIRMED, returns it unchanged (idempotent success)\n   - If status is CREATED, updates it to CONFIRMED and saves\n   - Returns the shipment in all success cases with ResponseEntity.ok()\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt**: Add four new test methods:\n   - `confirms a created shipment` - verify CREATED → CONFIRMED transition\n   - `confirms an already confirmed shipment` - verify idempotency (no change, still succeeds)\n   - `rejects confirming a cancelled shipment with conflict` - verify 409 on cancelled\n   - `rejects confirming a nonexistent shipment with not found` - verify 404 on missing\n\n**Alternative rejected**:\n- Could reuse existing ErrorCode like SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS for cancelled state, but that's semantically incorrect and violates the \"consistent with the rest of this API\" criterion. Each error code should describe a specific condition.\n- Could implement confirm logic in repository layer, but following the existing pattern (create logic in controller), the business logic belongs in the controller with repository as data store.\n\n**Data and error flow**:\n- Success: GET shipment from repo → check status → update if CREATED → save to repo → return 200 with shipment\n- Idempotent: GET shipment from repo → already CONFIRMED → return 200 with unchanged shipment\n- Cancelled error: GET shipment from repo → is CANCELLED → throw ConflictException → GlobalExceptionHandler catches → return 409 with ApiError envelope {code: SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS}\n- Not found error: GET from repo returns null → throw ResourceNotFoundException → GlobalExceptionHandler catches → return 404 with ApiError envelope {code: SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND}\n\n**Test strategy**:\n1. Test 1: Create shipment (CREATED), confirm it, assert status is CONFIRMED and response is 200\n2. Test 2: Create and confirm a shipment, confirm again, assert still CONFIRMED with 200\n3. Test 3: Create shipment, manually set status to CANCELLED in repository, attempt confirm, assert 409 with error code SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS\n4. Test 4: Attempt to confirm non-existent shipment, assert 404 with error code SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n```\n\nNow I'll implement the changes:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2877,"cache_read_input_tokens":18016,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2877},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3fa10487-97c4-4447-b1d2-cf8e4db8d175","uuid":"cae02023-1594-4838-bfdb-5ac757c99c1e","timestamp":"2026-09-30T15:00:52.703Z","request_id":"req_011CfZpkQkvJcUUHqo2uZiah"}
